WEBVTT

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:09.949
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Tuesday the twenty-eighth. Can you all hear me, or am I talking to myself again?</v>

00:00:10.929 --> 00:00:15.830
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, we can hear you. More importantly, there's a birthday cake in the office.</v>

00:00:16.649 --> 00:00:22.600
<v Sarah Okafor>There is a birthday cake in the office, and apparently that's the main production news this morning.</v>

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:27.629
<v David Whitfield>Depends how many slices you're counting as a batch.</v>

00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:34.500
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, before this becomes a cake allocation meeting. What's already out of the way?</v>

00:00:34.990 --> 00:00:41.289
<v David Whitfield>I already swapped the filter on the line 3 screw yesterday. That's finished, not another one for today.</v>

00:00:41.950 --> 00:00:45.100
<v Callum Reid>Ah, right. I was looking at yesterday's note, then.</v>

00:00:46.670 --> 00:00:53.320
<v Sarah Okafor>Yeah. Separate issue, though: the supplier still hasn't confirmed the delivery for the line 3 screw. That's still blocked.</v>

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:58.369
<v Fiona Doyle>So the delivery's unresolved, but the filter work is done. Two separate bits.</v>

00:00:59.079 --> 00:01:02.929
<v David Whitfield>Exactly. Don't want the filter swap following me round all week.</v>

00:01:04.019 --> 00:01:09.269
<v Grace Liu>And I already swapped the filter on the dryer yesterday. That one's finished as well.</v>

00:01:11.609 --> 00:01:13.359
<v Priya Raman>Yeah, saw that marked complete.</v>

00:01:15.430 --> 00:01:19.629
<v Grace Liu>Lovely. Just making sure it doesn't get read back as new work.</v>

00:01:20.099 --> 00:01:25.349
<v Sarah Okafor>PR, can you sort the training records for the new starters this morning? No rush.</v>

00:01:27.219 --> 00:01:32.120
<v Priya Raman>Um, yeah. No rush as in not an immediate interruption, but still this morning?</v>

00:01:33.340 --> 00:01:36.140
<v Sarah Okafor>Exactly. This morning, just not a drop-everything job.</v>

00:01:36.670 --> 00:01:40.870
<v Priya Raman>Fine, I'll sort the training records for the new starters this morning.</v>

00:01:42.129 --> 00:01:44.930
<v Fiona Doyle>Got you. Morning deadline, without the panic attached.</v>

00:01:46.739 --> 00:01:54.090
<v Sarah Okafor>Fi, can you write up the near miss at the line one? Due tomorrow, but that one's safety critical, straight away.</v>

00:01:54.530 --> 00:01:58.730
<v Fiona Doyle>Yeah, I'll start straight away and have the write-up done by tomorrow.</v>

00:02:00.060 --> 00:02:04.959
<v Grace Liu>Yeah, the safety-critical bit matters there. Tomorrow isn't a reason to leave it sitting.</v>

00:02:06.209 --> 00:02:09.360
<v Sarah Okafor>That's what I mean. Immediate attention, write-up due tomorrow.</v>

00:02:10.620 --> 00:02:13.419
<v Fiona Doyle>Understood. I've got the line one near miss.</v>

00:02:14.860 --> 00:02:20.110
<v Callum Reid>While we're on the lines—sorry, were you finished? What's the scope on the robot jam?</v>

00:02:20.590 --> 00:02:29.340
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep. Callum, can you clear the jam and check the sensors on the Line 2 Pick and Place Robot? It matters but it's not urgent.</v>

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:37.400
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, I'll clear the jam and check the sensors on the Line 2 Pick and Place Robot. Both bits, understood.</v>

00:02:37.750 --> 00:02:41.250
<v David Whitfield>That's the physical job, not the purchase order discussion, yeah?</v>

00:02:41.580 --> 00:02:45.780
<v Sarah Okafor>Correct. Callum's taking the jam and sensor check, not the purchasing bit.</v>

00:02:47.360 --> 00:02:56.810
<v Fiona Doyle>That purchasing bit does still need someone to chase the purchase order for the pick and place on two. Not an emergency but don't let it slip.</v>

00:02:59.080 --> 00:03:01.180
<v Sarah Okafor>Anyone able to take that one?</v>

00:03:02.569 --> 00:03:08.870
<v Priya Raman>Not me, sorry. I can take the records, but I'm not taking the purchase order chase as well.</v>

00:03:11.270 --> 00:03:16.870
<v Fiona Doyle>I haven't got room for it either. Raising it isn't me volunteering, just to be clear.</v>

00:03:19.349 --> 00:03:24.949
<v Sarah Okafor>Fair enough. Nobody's taken it, then. It's still needed and unowned; let's not pretend it's covered.</v>

00:03:26.870 --> 00:03:35.270
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, so, on mine: I'll recalibrate the sensors on the line 3 chiller by tomorrow morning. Not an emergency but don't let it slip.</v>

00:03:37.479 --> 00:03:41.330
<v David Whitfield>Sorry, sensors on the chiller? Teams clipped the middle of that.</v>

00:03:42.979 --> 00:03:45.780
<v Marcus Hale>The line 3 chiller, yeah. Recalibrating the sensors.</v>

00:03:47.129 --> 00:03:53.430
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, Marcus Hale has that, due tomorrow morning. Not an emergency, but it needs to stay on track.</v>

00:03:55.300 --> 00:03:56.500
<v Marcus Hale>Yep, that's mine.</v>

00:03:57.580 --> 00:04:01.780
<v Grace Liu>I'll inspect the booster pump for leaks as well. By next Tuesday.</v>

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:10.139
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Grace. Drop everything for that one. The due point is next Tuesday, but it's the top-priority one.</v>

00:04:11.909 --> 00:04:17.860
<v Grace Liu>Understood. I'll treat the booster pump inspection as drop-everything priority and get it done by next Tuesday.</v>

00:04:18.850 --> 00:04:22.350
<v Callum Reid>Sorry—next Tuesday, not today? Just checking I heard the date.</v>

00:04:23.430 --> 00:04:27.279
<v Grace Liu>Next Tuesday is the deadline, yes. The priority doesn't change that.</v>

00:04:29.560 --> 00:04:32.360
<v Sarah Okafor>Right. Urgency and due date both captured, then.</v>

00:04:34.069 --> 00:04:37.569
<v Grace Liu>And I'll run the monthly fire alarm test on Friday.</v>

00:04:39.029 --> 00:04:42.879
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, Grace Liu for the monthly fire alarm test on Friday.</v>

00:04:43.519 --> 00:04:44.920
<v Grace Liu>Yep, I'll do that.</v>

00:04:45.730 --> 00:04:53.079
<v Fiona Doyle>On alarms, just an observation: noticed the Fire Alarm Panel was running a bit warm on nights but it settled down.</v>

00:04:54.790 --> 00:04:58.990
<v Priya Raman>It settled down, yeah? You're not raising a separate job off that?</v>

00:05:00.790 --> 00:05:06.389
<v Fiona Doyle>No, just passing on what was noticed. It settled down. Not asking for another job today.</v>

00:05:08.060 --> 00:05:12.959
<v Marcus Hale>Good to distinguish it. Otherwise the word 'alarm' gets said and everyone stops breathing.</v>

00:05:15.129 --> 00:05:19.329
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, quick check of what's actually agreed, rather than everything we've mentioned.</v>

00:05:21.500 --> 00:05:26.050
<v David Whitfield>Nothing new against me. The line 3 screw filter was yesterday's finished work.</v>

00:05:28.029 --> 00:05:33.629
<v Sarah Okafor>Yes, and the supplier delivery is still a blocker, not a fresh action we've allocated here.</v>

00:05:35.149 --> 00:05:42.500
<v Callum Reid>I've got the Line 2 Pick and Place Robot jam and sensors. Matters, not urgent. No purchase order attached to me.</v>

00:05:42.860 --> 00:05:47.060
<v Priya Raman>Training records for the new starters, this morning, no rush. That's mine.</v>

00:05:47.860 --> 00:05:53.110
<v Fiona Doyle>And mine's the line one near miss write-up. Safety critical, starting straight away, due tomorrow.</v>

00:05:53.990 --> 00:06:00.990
<v Marcus Hale>Line 3—sorry, the line 3 chiller sensors for me. Recalibrated by tomorrow morning. Not an emergency, won't let it slip.</v>

00:06:02.709 --> 00:06:08.660
<v Grace Liu>Booster pump leak inspection, drop-everything priority, by next Tuesday. And the monthly fire alarm test on Friday.</v>

00:06:09.019 --> 00:06:18.470
<v Sarah Okafor>Only loose one is chasing the purchase order for the pick and place on two. Not an emergency but don't let it slip; still nobody owning it.</v>

00:06:18.920 --> 00:06:22.769
<v Fiona Doyle>Yeah, leave that visibly unowned. We haven't agreed someone for it.</v>

00:06:25.019 --> 00:06:27.819
<v Callum Reid>Right. At least the cake's got universal support.</v>

00:06:29.699 --> 00:06:33.899
<v Sarah Okafor>First unanimous decision of the morning. Cheers, everyone, we'll leave it there.</v>
